  "notes": "Cash-basis village with governmental activities and one enterprise (water/sewer) fund. Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (p4) Total column; business-type lines from the Proprietary Fund statement (p6). Governmental fund balances equal cash (beginning 970,393, ending 1,268,075). Transfers in/(out) between General (69,149 out) and Special Revenue (69,149 in) net to zero in the Total column (p4), so transfers_in/out are null. Business-type reported receipts = operating 418,178 + non-operating (106,494) summed by me (no single printed total); non-operating miscellaneous is negative (112,152). Business-type 'Charges for services' Sewer/Water shown as printed on p6 (Water 116,487; statement of activities p2 shows 117,687 = 116,487 + licenses/fees 1,200). Balance sheet (attempt 2, user rule 2026-10-27): governmental lines from the governmental funds Balance Sheet - Cash Basis (p3, Total column; totals 1,268,075 equal the government-wide governmental column), fund balance by classification (Committed: Debt service/Street/Community betterment, Unassigned); business-type lines from the Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1); totals are the p1 Total column. No liabilities (cash basis). Detail: budget-and-actual schedules for General, Special Revenue and Debt Service funds (pp7-9); no enterprise-fund budget schedule in the trimmed PDF. Special Revenue 'Motor vehicle' 33,315 categorized Motor Vehicle Pro-Rate (p4 shows it as Motor vehicle prorate). Budgetary-basis actuals differ from the fund statement (e.g. General property taxes 409,571 includes homestead 17,911; budgetary revenues include net transfers for Special Revenue). Attempt 3 (charges re-check 2026-10-29): Enterprise Fund 'Charges for services: Sewer' 301,691 and 'Water' 116,487 recategorized to Utility Charges (user rule 2026-10-28); governmental 'Charges for services' 158,693 (general government, public safety, culture per p2) stays charges for services; Special Revenue budget 'Other local receipts' 60,365 stays charges for services (59,920 charges + 445 interest per p4; not split since the budget schedule prints no breakdown). Read pages 1-9 of 9"
}
